FRANCHISE = [
 ("Inventory & Reorder Policy", "Operations SOP", "Every outlet keeps a safety stock equal to three days of average demand. A reorder is raised when days of cover fall below the supplier lead time plus two days. Perishables follow FEFO rotation: the earliest expiry is sold first and anything within 24 hours of expiry is marked down 30 percent or written off. Stock-outs of a top-10 SKU for more than 6 hours must be escalated to the regional manager. Suppliers with lead time above 5 days need a secondary supplier on file. Purchase orders above 2 lakh rupees need owner approval; below that the Store Manager may approve."),
 ("Staffing, Overtime & Attrition Policy", "HR Manual", "Staff may work at most 48 hours a week; overtime beyond 9 hours a week is flagged and needs Store Manager approval, beyond 16 hours the Franchise Owner. An outlet must keep at least 85 percent of its rostered staff present on weekends. Three unexplained absences in a month trigger a counselling meeting. Attrition risk above 70 percent from the model prompts a retention conversation within 7 days: review pay band, schedule fairness and growth path. New hires complete food-safety induction before their first solo shift."),
 ("Food Safety & FSSAI Compliance", "Compliance", "Every outlet must display a valid FSSAI licence. Cold storage stays between 1 and 4 degrees Celsius, deep freezers below minus 18. Cooking oil is discarded when total polar compounds exceed 25 percent. A failed internal audit (score below 60) requires a corrective action plan in 48 hours and a re-audit within 14 days. Critical violations such as pest evidence or temperature abuse close the affected station immediately. Audit records are retained for 24 months."),
 ("Customer Service & CSAT Standard", "Service SOP", "Outlets maintain a CSAT of at least 4.0 out of 5. Customers are greeted within 30 seconds and complaints resolved within 24 hours. An outlet whose rolling sentiment score falls below 45 out of 100 enters service recovery: manager call-back to unhappy customers, a shift briefing on the top complaint theme, and a mystery-shopper visit within 10 days. Review replies must be polite, specific and never blame the customer. Refunds up to 500 rupees can be granted by the shift lead."),
 ("Marketing Campaign & Discount Guardrails", "Marketing Policy", "Discounts above 25 percent need Franchise Owner approval. Campaigns must show positive uplift within the first 14 days or be paused: uplift is measured against the same weekday baseline. Promotions may not be run on items with fewer than 2 days of stock cover. Local campaigns spend at most 3 percent of monthly sales. Loyalty offers are capped at one per customer per day. Every campaign records its target outlets, start date and expected lift."),
 ("Outlet Performance & Health Score", "Franchise Agreement", "Each outlet receives a health score from 0 to 100 combining sales trend, inventory cover, staffing, audit results and sentiment. Below 60 is critical: the owner reviews it weekly. Below 80 is warning. Two consecutive critical months trigger a performance improvement plan with a 60-day window. Royalty is 5 percent of net sales, paid monthly; late payment attracts 1.5 percent per month. Franchisees must submit daily sales through the POS feed."),
 ("Incident Escalation & Approval Matrix", "Operations SOP", "Agent-raised tickets follow severity: Info is handled within 72 hours, Warning within 24 hours, Critical within 4 hours. Critical tickets are assigned to the Franchise Owner when unowned for 1 hour. Actions that spend money or contact customers (purchase orders, discounts, messages) require human approval; read-only checks and internal notes are automatic. Every approval and rejection is written to the audit log with the approver and time."),
 ("Data Privacy & Employee Records", "Compliance", "Customer phone numbers and e-mail addresses are used only for service and consented marketing. Employee records are visible to the Store Manager of that outlet and the Franchise Owner only. Exports containing personal data are logged. Data is retained for at most 24 months unless law requires longer. A data-subject request must be answered within 30 days."),
]
