 ("Weather & Storm Response", "Safety Manual", "Wind above 17 m/s or wave height above 4 metres is a Warning for the affected leg; wind above 25 m/s is Critical and the master may deviate. Vessels within 500 nautical miles of a named storm are re-evaluated every 6 hours. Cargo sensitive to temperature or moisture carries extra weather insurance during monsoon and typhoon seasons. Deviation costs are recorded against the shipment and shared with the customer."),
